    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43960" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐθενία</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐθένεια</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i> (q.v.), from which it cannot be distd. after <span class="entity">ii
			B.C.</span>: 
				Ion.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐθενίη</span></b>  (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">¯̆</span>) Epigr. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rev.Phil.</u>
				19.178
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
				1036.19
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Nicomedia</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐθενία</span> is v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1360b16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>HA</u>
				602a15
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐσθένεια, εὐθένεια</span>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Gaur.</u>
				16.2
			</span></i>.—From <span class="entity">ii A.D.</span>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐθένεια</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐθενία</span> begin to be confused with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐθηνία</span>.</div>
